<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.jambi.retirement-tunnel — this project's own cloudflared process.

  A SEPARATE tunnel from the trading desk's, on purpose. Sharing one means
  sharing its ingress file (which is tracked in the trading-helper repo, so an
  edit breaks that repo's `git pull --ff-only`) and sharing its restarts. Two
  processes cost a few MB and remove the coupling entirely.

  Do NOT point this at the trading tunnel's id. Two processes running the same
  tunnel both connect, each with its own ingress list, and Cloudflare picks
  between them per request -- so the site would work roughly half the time,
  which is worse than not working at all.

  KeepAlive, and the config is read from this repo. cloudflared re-reads its
  config on SIGHUP; a full restart here never touches the trading tunnel.

  It execs scripts/run_tunnel.sh rather than resolving the binary inline. A
  PATH lookup inside a plist is both fragile and undebuggable -- when it fails
  you get Cloudflare error 1033 and no reason anywhere. The script searches
  explicit locations, logs which one it chose, and names what was missing.

  NO SHELL. This job needs no profile at all, so it does not ask for one: the
  script finds cloudflared itself. Note for the other agents -- `zsh -lc` reads
  .zshenv/.zprofile/.zlogin but NOT .zshrc, which is where most PATH edits
  actually live, so no login shell is a reliable way to find a binary. Pinned
  absolute paths are.

  Install: scripts/install_agents.sh
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.jambi.retirement-tunnel</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/jambimac/repo/retirement/scripts/run_tunnel.sh</string>
  </array>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/jambimac/repo/retirement/logs/tunnel.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/jambimac/repo/retirement/logs/tunnel.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
